---
description: Harmony project rules — always applied
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root before making changes. It is the single
source of instructions for all AI tools here and is deliberately short.

Key rules, repeated so they are always in context:

- All server config lives in `server/_core/env.ts`. Never read `process.env`
  elsewhere on the server.
- Log via `server/_core/logger.ts`, never `console.*`.
- One domain per file in `server/routers/`; register it in `server/routers/index.ts`.
- Never return `passwordHash` (or any credential column) to a client — use
  `toPublicUser()` from `server/routers/_shared.ts`.
- Never commit secrets. Doppler locally, Vercel env vars when deployed.
- Run `pnpm verify` (typecheck + test + build) before declaring work complete.
- Update `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` and `docs/CHANGELOG.md` when you finish work.

Do not read `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `client/src/components/ui/**`, `attached_assets/`,
`docs/archive/**`, or `client/src/pages/ComponentShowcase.tsx` — they are large and
carry no signal. Use `docs/architecture/repo-map.md` to locate code instead of
searching broadly.
